  "summary": "Auto-executing reconnaissance loop against third-party host from installer's IP",
  "details": "Package's main entry (payload.js) is an IIFE that runs immediately on require/import. On load it fetches a ~3600-entry wordlist of Linux binary names (including offensive tooling such as aircrack-ng, beef, burpsuitepro, bully, ffuf) and issues concurrent HEAD probes against https://entretienextremejb.ca/bin/<name>, enumerating that third-party host from the installer's network identity. There is no advertised library function; the sole load-time behavior is outbound reconnaissance traffic attributed to the installer.",
